{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962310,"nonce":"yADdfZ8uZ9sbz/9aq9PQxUl5xRA=","title":"Zig grammar: a mutable global var lowers as a read-only DynamicBox constant, so storing to it faults","message":"A Zig-grammar global `var failure: i64 = 0;` lowers as `const @failure: *opaque(DynamicBox)`, so a store to it from the interpreter faults on read-only memory. A var global should lower as a mutable global of its declared type (i64), not a boxed constant. Seen by caribou while writing the take_pending_error test (08b2b443).","files":null}]}